{"t": 1794106594.9316597, "kind": "call", "tool": "slack_post_message", "args": {"channel_id": "C07INCID003", "text": "*Checkout paging \u2014 PaymentGatewayErrors (AG-7731, critical)*\n\n*Impact:* ~38% of checkout gateway charge calls returning 4xx since 07:41 UTC.\n*Cause:* Gateway API 2026-11 (\"strict amounts\") went live at 07:41 UTC and now requires `amount` as an integer in minor units (cents). `checkout/gateway.py` still sent a fractional-euro float (`12.34`), so the gateway rejected every charge: `400 {\"error\":\"invalid_amount\",\"message\":\"amount must be an integer in minor units (cents), got 12.34\"}`.\n*Fix:* `charge_payload()` now converts EUR to integer cents using Decimal with ROUND_HALF_UP (avoids float truncation, e.g. `12.34*100 == 1233.99...`). Signature unchanged, so callers need no changes. Verified: 12.34 -> 1234, 19.99 -> 1999, 2.675 -> 268.\n*Next:* deploy checkout, then watch the 4xx rate return to baseline and confirm no `invalid_amount` in Loki. No Sentry issues were raised for this (4xx, not exceptions)."}, "ok": true}
